[00:00:00.000] The Control Center Interface.
The Apple iPhone Control Center interface occupies substantially the entire display. The interface consists of a status area at the top of the display, multiple grouped system controls and indicators arranged in a grid, and a vertical column of interface icons positioned along the right edge of the display.
Status Area
•	At the top of the display, from left to right, the following elements are visible:
o	A plus ("+") symbol positioned in the upper-left corner.
o	The Dynamic Island is centered at the top of the display. A solid red circular indicator is visible toward its left side, consistent with the iOS screen-recording status indicator.
o	A power symbol positioned in the upper-right corner.
o	
•	Immediately below the status area are:
o	An Airplane Mode status indicator positioned on the left.
o	A battery indicator positioned on the right displaying a battery level of 2%.
The Connectivity Module
The upper-left Control Center module contains a group of connectivity-related controls arranged within a rounded rectangular panel.
•	The following controls are displayed:
o	Airplane Mode, displayed as an orange circular button with a white airplane symbol, visually indicating an active or enabled state.
o	AirDrop, displayed as a gray circular button with a white AirDrop symbol, indicating an inactive state.
o	Wi-Fi, displayed as a gray circular button containing a Wi-Fi symbol with a diagonal slash through the symbol, indicating an inactive state.
o	Four additional gray circular controls displaying symbols visually consistent with:
	Cellular communications, indicating a disabled state.
	Bluetooth, indicating an inactive state.
	Hot spot, indicating a disabled state.
	VPN, indicating a disabled state.
The Media Playback Module
The upper-right Control Center module contains the media playback controls.
•	The module displays:
o	An empty media artwork placeholder positioned on the left side.
o	An AirPlay output icon positioned in the upper-right corner, indicating an inactive state.
o	The text "Not Playing" displayed beneath the artwork placeholder.
o	A row of media playback controls consisting of:
	Previous.
	Play.
	Next.
o	The module displays no media title, artist information, or artwork.

The Rotation Lock and Silent Mode Controls
Immediately below the Connectivity Module are two circular system controls.
•	These controls display symbols visually consistent with:
o	Rotation Lock: Displayed as a gray circular button containing an open padlock with a curved arrow, indicating the rotation lock feature is inactive.
o	Silent Mode: Displayed as a white circular button containing a red bell symbol with a diagonal slash through it, indicating the phone is in silent mode.

The Focus Module
Positioned below the Rotation Lock and Silent Mode controls is a rounded rectangular module labeled "Focus."
The module contains multiple small circular icons representing available Focus modes together with a downward-pointing disclosure indicator.
The Brightness and Volume Controls
Immediately below the Media Playback Module are two vertical slider controls.
•	The left slider controls screen brightness and displays a sun symbol near its lower end. The brightness level is approximately 30% up.
•	The right slider controls system volume and displays a speaker symbol near its lower end. The volume level is approximately 47% up.
The Utility Controls
The lower portion of the Control Center contains eight circular system controls arranged in two rows of four controls each.
•	The controls display symbols visually consistent with:
o	Flashlight.
o	Timer.
o	Calculator.
o	Camera.
o	Screen Mirroring.
o	Code Scanner (QR Scanner).
o	Screen Recording: displaying a red circular recording indicator within the control.
o	Notes / Quick Note.

The Right-Edge Interface Icons
Along the right edge of the display is a vertical column of three interface icons. From top to bottom, the icons consist of:
•	A heart symbol (Favorites/Home group, the current one).
•	A musical note symbol (Media Playback group).
•	A wireless transmission symbol (Connectivity group)
