[00:00:07.140] Control Center Expansion Gesture: The video depicts an extended downward swipe gesture within the Control Center interface, resulting in a continuous transition across multiple modular sub-screens.
Initial Scale & Media Player Phase: The gesture initially reveals the primary Control Center interface at a reduced scale. As the swipe continues downward, the heart icon from the right-hand stack transitions to white, increases slightly in size, and shifts leftward.
[00:00:07.272] Media Player View: The display transitions to the dedicated media player interface (featuring an iPod graphic displaying "Not Playing"). During this phase, the musical note icon in the right-hand stack enlarges, changes from gray to white, and shifts leftward, while the heart icon returns to its original size, color, and position.
[00:00:07.437] Connectivity Panel View: Continuing the downward motion, the wireless transmission symbol enlarges, turns white, and shifts leftward while the musical note returns to its default appearance. 
[00:00:08.196] The interface finally settles on the full-screen connectivity panel.
•	Connectivity Panel Layout: The interface displays a vertically arranged series of rounded rectangular control panels set against a blurred background:
•	Airplane Mode: Full-width control at the top labeled “Airplane Mode” with status “On,” featuring an airplane symbol inside an orange circular icon on the left.
•	Wi-Fi: Left-hand control labeled “Wi-Fi” displaying “Off,” with a Wi-Fi symbol inside a gray circular icon.
•	AirDrop: Right-hand control labeled “AirDrop” displaying “Receiving Off,” with an AirDrop symbol inside a gray circular icon.
•	Cellular Data: Left-hand control labeled “Cellular Data” displaying “Off,” with its corresponding icon in a muted gray disabled state, visually distinct from standard inactive states due to low-contrast color rendering of both the cell icon shape and its surrounding containment circle.
•	Bluetooth: Right-hand control labeled “Bluetooth” displaying “Off,” with a Bluetooth symbol inside a gray circular icon.
•	Personal Hotspot: Full-width control labeled “Personal Hotspot” displaying “Off,” with its associated icon in a muted gray disabled state, visually distinct from standard inactive states due to low-contrast color rendering of both the hotspot icon shape and its surrounding containment circle.
•	VPN: Full-width control at the bottom of the visible interface labeled “VPN” displaying “Off,” with a VPN-related icon in a muted gray disabled state, visually distinct from standard inactive states due to low-contrast color rendering of both the VPN icon shape and its surrounding containment circle.
[00:00:09.582] Reverse Transition & Settling Phase: As the downward swipe concludes and the interface fully engages the main panel, the sequence reverses direction to settle into the primary view.
Initial Retraction Phase: Releasing or finalizing the downward motion prompts the interface to retrace its steps upward. The wireless transmission symbol shrinks, and shifts rightward. Then, it enlarges again as it shifts left.
[00:00:09.615] The view briefly cycles back through the dedicated media player interface.
The musical note changes from gray to white, and it enlarges as it shifts left, while the transmission symbol shrinks, and shifts rightward.
[00:00:09.780] As the upward settling continues, the musical note icon returns to its original size, color, and position, while the heart icon from the right-hand stack scales up, transitions to white, and shifts leftward.
[00:00:10.473] The iPhone "Control Center" interface main view is displayed fully.
[00:00:10.638] The Control Center is swiped upward out of view.
